@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+This document records how privacy is built into the site and how to keep it that way.
+Run the automated check before every release:
+
+```sh
+pnpm run audit:privacy
+```
+
+## 1. Principles applied
+
+| Principle | Implementation |
+|---|---|
+| **Proactive, not reactive** | `scripts/privacy-audit.mjs` fails the build on third-party origins, trackers, unsafe inline code, insecure forms, or missing headers. |
+| **Privacy as the default** | No optional storage or telemetry runs until the user opts in. Without JavaScript nothing optional exists at all. Global Privacy Control / Do Not Track are honoured as a binding opt-out and lock the choices off. |
+| **Embedded into design** | All assets are first-party (the hero photo is self-hosted, so visitors' IPs/Referers are no longer sent to Unsplash). A strict CSP (`default-src 'none'`) enforces this in the browser. |
+| **Full functionality** | Reject and Accept have equal weight. Reject is one click, and choices can be changed any time via the footer "Privacy Choices" button. |
+| **End-to-end security** | HSTS, CSP, COOP/COEP/CORP, `nosniff`, `frame-ancestors 'none'`, `Clear-Site-Data` on logout, `no-store` on personalised pages. Logout is now a POST. |
+| **Visibility & transparency** | Plain-language banner, per-category descriptions, retention periods, and this document. |
+| **Respect for the user** | Consent expires after 180 days and is re-requested when purposes change (`consentVersion`). Withdrawing consent purges the related data immediately. |
+
+## 2. Data inventory (client side)
+
+| Data | Where | Category | Retention | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Consent record `dg_consent` | localStorage | Strictly necessary | 180 days | Stores category booleans, schema version and the date only (no time, no ID). |
+| `dg_preferences:*` | localStorage | Preferences (opt-in) | ≤180 days per item | Written only via `DailyGrindPrivacy.storage`. Purged when consent is withdrawn. Must never hold PII. |
+| Page-view beacon | `POST /api/metrics` | Analytics (opt-in) | Server-defined (aggregate only) | Payload is `{event, path}` with numeric/hash/email path segments generalised. No cookies, ID, referrer, UA, screen or timezone. |
+| Session cookie | Server | Strictly necessary | Session | Server must set `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` (or `Strict`) and invalidate the session on `POST /logout`. |
+
+Anything not in this table must not be collected. Add a row (with purpose and retention) before introducing new data.
+
+## 3. Client-side controls (`assets/js/privacy.js`)
+
+- **Tracking-parameter stripping**: `utm_*`, `gclid`, `fbclid`, `msclkid`, etc. are removed from the address bar and from links on click.
+- **Outbound links**: get `rel="noopener noreferrer"` and `referrerpolicy="no-referrer"`.
+- **Runtime third-party audit**: `PerformanceObserver` + `MutationObserver` flag any resource from an origin outside the allow-list, and CSP violations are logged. Only the origin is recorded, after redaction. Inspect with `DailyGrindPrivacy.auditReport()`.
+- **Data minimisation helpers**: `redact()` scrubs emails, card numbers, phone numbers, SSNs, IPs and tokens. `minimize(obj, allowList)` keeps only the allow-listed keys. `coarsePath()` generalises IDs.
+- **Secure forms**: blocks GET submissions containing sensitive fields and submissions to other origins. Drops empty `data-optional` fields. Sets `autocomplete="off"` on `cc-csc`. Clears password/card/`data-sensitive` fields on `pagehide` (bfcache).
+- **Storage hygiene**: expired, unknown or non-consented `dg_*` keys are swept on every load. Corrupted entries are discarded.
+
+## 4. Security headers
+
+- **Production**: `_headers` (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages syntax). Mirror these settings in any other CDN or reverse proxy.
+- **Local**: `pnpm start` passes `--csp` and `--coi` to statikk.
+- **Fallback**: `index.html` carries a matching `<meta>` CSP and referrer policy as defence-in-depth. The audit checks that the meta CSP and header CSP stay in sync. `frame-ancestors` only works as a header.
+
+## 5. Third-party audit
+
+**Current status (2026-11-08): zero third parties.**
+
+| Previously found | Risk | Action |
+|---|---|---|
+| `images.unsplash.com` hero image (CSS background) | Each visit sent the visitor's IP, user agent and Referer to a third party. It was also incompatible with COEP/strict CSP. | Downloaded to `assets/img/hero-coffee.jpg` (Unsplash License; checked for EXIF/GPS metadata, none present). |
+
+No analytics, fonts, ads, tag managers, social widgets or embeds are used.
+
+### Third-party review checklist
+
+Before adding any origin to `privacy/third-parties.json`:
+
+1. Is it necessary? Can it be self-hosted instead (fonts, libraries, images)?
+2. What data does it receive (IP, cookies, identifiers, page content)? Record this as `dataShared`.
+3. What is the legal basis? If it needs consent, gate it behind `DailyGrindPrivacy.hasConsent(...)` and do not load it before consent.
+4. Is a DPA signed (`dpaSigned: true`)? Where is data processed and transferred?
+5. Scripts must be pinned with Subresource Integrity and `crossorigin="anonymous"`.
+6. Update the CSP in `_headers`, `index.html` and `package.json`, plus `allowedOrigins` in `privacy.js`.
+7. Set `reviewedOn` and re-review at least yearly (the audit warns when `lastReviewed` is more than 365 days old).
+
+## 6. Server-side requirements (outside this repo)
+
+- Implement `POST /logout`: verify `Origin`, destroy the session, respond with `Clear-Site-Data`.
+- Session cookies: `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite`, with the `__Host-` prefix.
+- `/api/metrics` must not log IP addresses or user agents, and should store aggregate counts only.
+- Honour the `Sec-GPC: 1` request header server-side as well.
